{"name":"Sheikh Zayed White","hex":"#e6efef","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sheikh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The leader of an Arab village, family or small tribe.","An Islamic religious cleric; the master of a Sufi order."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheikh"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan","blocks":[{"text":"Sheikh Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan was an Emirati politician, philanthropist, and the founding father of the United Arab Emirates. Zayed served as the governor of Eastern Region from 1946 until he became the ruler of Abu Dhabi in 1966, and served as the first president of the United Arab Emirates from its independence on 2 December 1971 until his death in 2004. He is referred in the United Arab Emirates as the Father of the Nation for being the principal driving force behind the unification of the United Arab Emirates."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/Sheikh_Zayed_with_King_Faisal%2C_1974_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zayed_bin_Sultan_Al_Nahyan","wikidata":"Q167846"},{"title":"Sheikh","blocks":[{"text":"Sheikh is an honorific title in the Arabic language, literally meaning \"elder\". It commonly designates a tribal chief or a Muslim scholar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/UsulALFiqh.svg/330px-UsulALFiqh.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheikh","wikidata":"Q185166"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Khalifa_and_Zayed_Al_Nahyan.jpg/500px-Khalifa_and_Zayed_Al_Nahyan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Khalifa_and_Zayed_Al_Nahyan.jpg/500px-Khalifa_and_Zayed_Al_Nahyan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sheikh Zayed next to his son Sheikh Khalifa in 1971","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKhalifa_and_Zayed_Al_Nahyan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Sheikh_Zayed_visiting_Kairouan.jpg/500px-Sheikh_Zayed_visiting_Kairouan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Sheikh_Zayed_visiting_Kairouan.jpg/1280px-Sheikh_Zayed_visiting_Kairouan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Sheikh_Zayed_visiting_Kairouan.jpg/500px-Sheikh_Zayed_visiting_Kairouan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm